-- and a rate set by how much of a named substance is dissolved: the order of magnitude of the rate is the
-- base rate plus the amount of the catalyst, which is what a first-order dependence on a concentration
-- looks like when both are read as orders of magnitude. A tag of its own per motion is what the previous
-- layer owed: this motion is catalysed by that substance and not by whatever happens to be in the bottle.
brate-catalysed : Nat → Nat → Bath → Nat
brate-catalysed tag base v = plus base (sol-amount tag (bath-sol v))
